# Theming / Corporate Design

A corporate styleguide exists for all user-facing surfaces. **Read it before writing or changing any styling.**

## Where the tokens live
SODa corporate design (Inter / Noto Sans, orange `#e68500`, menu-bar motif: orange dot + black rule). No separate `STYLEGUIDE.md` exists; the token sources are:

| Surface | Tokens | Build |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Public site + dashboard shell (`scs_custom_theme`) | `assets/scss/base/_vars.scss`, `_colors.scss`, `_typo.scss` | SCSS → `assets/css/styles.css` |
| Base reset, body font, cookie banner (`scs_custom_theme`) | `assets/css/reset.css`, `assets/css/cookie-banner.css` | plain CSS, no build |
| Manager UI (module `soda_scs_manager`, Tailwind v4) | `pcss/colors.pcss`, `@theme` blocks in `pcss/components/` | `npm run build` in the module → `css/soda-scs-manager.css` (no Node on the host: `node:22-alpine` container) |
| Keycloak login | `keycloak/keycloak/themes/scs/login/resources/css/scs-login.css` | container rebuild |
| SCS Health | `scs-health/app/globals.css` | container rebuild |

Read the relevant token file before styling. If a needed value is missing, ask instead of improvising.

## Hard rules
- **No new colors, fonts, radii, shadows, or spacing values.** Everything visual comes from the existing token system (CSS custom properties / `@theme` tokens). A raw hex value or arbitrary pixel size in component code is a defect.
- New UI (pages, buttons, nav, cards, forms) reuses the documented patterns: page-shell widths, typography scale, focus states, header/footer anatomy — do not design parallel variants of existing components.
- Both light and dark theme must be covered: every token used has a counterpart in both themes; never style only one mode.
- Accessibility is part of the design: visible focus styles, WCAG AA contrast for token pairs, state never conveyed by color alone.
- If a design need genuinely has no token or pattern, add the token to the central theme definition (and propose a styleguide update) — never inline the value.
